<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mithridates I of Pontus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 266 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Mithridates I Ktistes, Mithridates Ktistes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-i-of-parthia">Mithridates I</a> Ktistes, 'the Founder', was the first king of Pontus. A noble of Persian descent from the family that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cius">Kios</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a>, he escaped the wars of Alexander's successors around 302 BCE and established himself in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. He took the title king in 281 BCE, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amasya">Amaseia</a> and died in 266 BCE, leaving a dynasty that lasted until 63 BCE.</p></div>
